{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-28271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/7dc806c646f1e9f5edbfef789fbdc9dfca2745c637906bd61eccb8072440e8c0.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={63}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+2}{3x} \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-3x & =2 \\\\ 3x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1)} \\\\ x & =0.692\\,5…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x+2=3(0.692\\,5…)+2=4.077\\,6…, \\\\ AC & =3x=3(0.692\\,5…)=2.077\\,6….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(2.077\\,6…)(4.077\\,6…) \\\\  & =4.236\\,0… \\\\  & ≈4.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5104d1e4d0c4acb89e91fa4704372ec46397a7d9c2ad14bb4edce5547c8fb9c1"} {"question" "q-28271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3.8"] ["math" "4.2"] ["math" "4.7"] ["math" "5.3"] ["math" "6.3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4.2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/576323c48b707bb198045ab932342e53709c7a3678282835430e506c1a9dd605.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={45}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 6x & =5x+5 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =6x=6(5)=30, \\\\ BC & =5x+5=5(5)+5=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =450.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5104d1e4d0c4acb89e91fa4704372ec46397a7d9c2ad14bb4edce5547c8fb9c1"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "220"] ["math" "250"] ["math" "330"] ["math" "370"] ["math" "450"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-28319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "450"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/f1880dc62f774152ce5076a313928c0e8109ca174184704c5880891ed9243718.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2x+4}{6x+8} \\\\ 2(6x+8) & =5(2x+4) \\\\ 12x+16 & =10x+20 \\\\ 12x-10x & =20-16 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(2)+4=8, \\\\ AC & =6x+8=6(2)+8=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5104d1e4d0c4acb89e91fa4704372ec46397a7d9c2ad14bb4edce5547c8fb9c1"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "105"] ["math" "120"] ["math" "45"] ["math" "60"] ["math" "80"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-76770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "80"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/4572bd2ef8f6086ed80f5ac21e045e3cf2359680872a958a40d2f1e72f22d980.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{9x+2}{5x-1} \\\\ 2(5x-1) & =9x+2 \\\\ 10x-2 & =9x+2 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =9x+2=9(4)+2=38, \\\\ AC & =5x-1=5(4)-1=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 38\\cdot 19 \\\\  & =361.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5104d1e4d0c4acb89e91fa4704372ec46397a7d9c2ad14bb4edce5547c8fb9c1"} {"question" "q-251084" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251084" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "361"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/ba89c2cf139dd6251804ed0758c4edc4690463ba5ae14867549881a29736f9e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13} & =\\frac{12}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{12}{12}\\cdot 13 \\\\ AB & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{13}^{2}-{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169-144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5104d1e4d0c4acb89e91fa4704372ec46397a7d9c2ad14bb4edce5547c8fb9c1"} {"question" "q-251127" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"} {"question" "q-251127" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/state.json" "file_sha256" "a26abe9f9505dda1949fb2835bcf872a6a091cd05d487b7cf72827f2232be431"}] "usage" {"q-28271" []} "basis" 952 "retractions" [[17592186115596 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-28271.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186112977 17592186112978 17592186112979 17592186112980 17592186112981] "immutable_fields" [[17592186112976 :answer-field/correct] [17592186112976 :answer-field/id] [17592186112976 :answer-field/key] [17592186112976 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
